# Build output.
/target

# Local secrets and machine-specific settings.
.env

# macOS directory metadata.
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from the tools in tools/.
__pycache__/

# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this crate ships a binary, so the
# lockfile is what makes `cargo install --locked` reproduce a known-good build.
#
# There is deliberately no `testing/` entry. One used to live here, and because a
# pattern without a leading slash matches at every depth, it silently excluded
# `src/testing/` -- the entire unit test suite, which `#[cfg(test)] pub mod
# testing;` in src/lib.rs requires. A fresh clone therefore compiled but could
# not run a single test.
